{"title":"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many noncongruent integer-sided triangles with positive area and perimeter less than 15 are neither equilateral, isosceles, nor right triangles?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e6eb4ec63cefabf12bed1b9dea1b98b97920f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\; 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\; 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\; 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\; 6 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\; 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"346\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since we want non-congruent triangles that are neither isosceles nor equilateral, we can just list side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d9e22097e20a1249b5332202b24941a4bf9e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b,c)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/a/5ba70df5a2f9630194f32f50010cd2e78318c98d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;b&lt;c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"74\" height=\"13\" />. Furthermore, \"positive area\" tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e2bc45eeb61657ab7a4587926a2640593b0c26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c &lt; a + b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> and the perimeter constraints means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/f/a4ff1eaf0efa1741243226733302ff39d07ec99a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c &lt; 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"114\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>There are no triangles when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> because then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/91927ed6d1093e6ce84e3aa8446121218cb17b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, implying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/67176ff95b512b7db774dfb6fe8355e72df5dc96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\geq c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"17\" />, contrary to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e0917f060dc5c618be04a697a4801e83be2a7569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &lt; c$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55afdab16c8c49089c4d9ceeb8d3c8cf1f088be6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, similar to above, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd8ac52a9c6112e9ac737cba648d2c51efb97d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, so this leaves the only possibility <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/5/3850bfd552bec12638dd77153069f54ea0849bf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />. This gives 3 triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/d/e8d4dc7bb4863baee784beb8a61fe9800212633d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3,4), (2,4,5), (2,5,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"191\" height=\"20\" /> within our perimeter constraint.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340605c5f88cf6864adc5b146c3dffca7a45df22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/91927ed6d1093e6ce84e3aa8446121218cb17b71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/d/8cd8ac52a9c6112e9ac737cba648d2c51efb97d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, which gives triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6da01d976d1df29f088ae5bb7156a9e337fee514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,4,5), (3,4,6), (3,5,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/e/28eb10edb01b5d1369b1469e15dab327a4ad7b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,4,5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is a right triangle, so we get rid of it and we get only 2 triangles.\n</p><p>All in all, this gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/4/054046042412fb47232457a7fcb60b96400b22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+2 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\; 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"119\" height=\"28\" /> triangles.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B\">2015 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017235931\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 204/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2296/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4031/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.033      1 -total\n 62.22%    8.732      1 Template:AMC12_b